From 04bb2669ed7e413d7f5c86af20b6066aa82a4f82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Facenda <myrepo@facenda.uk>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 19:28:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: resolve execution-breaking and correctness bugs found in
 code scan

- plotting/multi_agent_plots: build lock-in annotation from the actual
  phenotype list instead of hardcoding three entries; two-agent cohorts
  (E6 preset) crashed plot generation with IndexError
- plotting/compare: restore make_compare_plot, deleted in the b28f70f
  plotting refactor while run_compare.py and make_compare_plot.py still
  imported it (ImportError at startup); panel wiring repaired so the
  Mean-VII panel actually plots mean_vii (it plotted watch time), the
  watch-time panel gets its bars, and the time-series panel separates
  agents with hue
- scripts/run_sweep: replace nonexistent User.clone() with build_user();
  sweeps with drift or interest updates enabled crashed with
  AttributeError and would otherwise leak user state across seeds
- simulation/engine: apply viewpoint drift using the resolved drift
  strength (drift_alpha wins, viewpoint_drift_rate fallback) as the
  resolver documents; callers passing only drift_alpha silently got no
  drift before
- scripts/run_compare: pass enable_viewpoint_drift/viewpoint_drift_rate
  through to the engine (drift_alpha was recorded in artefacts but drift
  was never applied), record the flag in the manifest, and build a fresh
  user per (agent, seed) so mutated state cannot leak across runs
- agents/deciders: supply the missing logger.debug arguments (unfilled
  %s placeholders caused logging errors at debug level)
- artefacts: correct _corpus_payload return annotation (list, not str)
- ui/views/explore_results: move module logger below imports (ruff E402)
- corpus/loader + corpus/generator: remove leftover development
  monologue comments and a duplicated dead 'video_pool' check; behaviour
  unchanged (corpus.seed default and generation order identical)
- runners/legacy_run_sweep: neutral wording for determinism comment
- configs/experiment_sweep.json: policy.mode 'llm' was silently ignored
  by the sweep runner (it never builds a decider); declare the heuristic
  mode that actually runs
- results/sweep_summary.csv: remove stale committed artefact; it used the
  removed legacy 'alpha' schema and cannot be regenerated by current code
  (.gitignore already excludes results/*.csv)
- tests: add regression tests for two-agent cohort plotting and for
  drift applied via drift_alpha only

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012anUZN7p7PaDUsmnarRq8Q
